<BaseLayout title="CV6 (Qihai) — Sea of Qi Point" description="Learn how to locate and stimulate CV6 (Qihai) — the Sea of Qi point. Benefits include vitality, digestive support, and immune system strengthening." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Points", href: "/points" }, { label: "CV6 (Qihai)", href: "/points/cv6-qihai-acupressure-point" }]} datePublished="2025-03-10" dateModified="2026-05-15" articleSchema={true}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6">
    <h1 class="mb-4">CV6 (Qihai) — Sea of Qi</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">CV6, known as Qihai or Sea of Qi, is one of the most important energy points on the body. Located on the lower abdomen, it is used for vitality, digestion, and immune strength.</p>

    <section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Location</h2>
    <img src="/images/cv6-location.webp" alt="CV6 acupressure point location on the lower abdomen" class="w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-xl shadow-sm" />
    <p class="mb-3">CV6 is on the midline of the lower abdomen, 1.5 cun (about two finger-widths) below the navel (umbilicus). It lies on the Conception Vessel (Ren Mai).</p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Benefits &amp; Uses</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Vitality and energy:</strong> CV6 restores Qi and is used for general fatigue, weakness, and debility.</li>
      <li><strong>Digestive health:</strong> It strengthens digestion, relieves bloating, and helps with chronic diarrhea.</li>
      <li><strong>Immune support:</strong> Regular stimulation of CV6 is believed to strengthen Wei Qi (defensive energy) and resistance to illness.</li>
      <li><strong>Reproductive health:</strong> CV6 supports reproductive organs and is used for menstrual irregularities and fertility support.</li>
      <li><strong>Emotional grounding:</strong> It helps with feelings of emptiness, insecurity, and lack of grounding.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">How to Massage CV6</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Lie on your back with your abdomen relaxed and uncovered.</li>
      <li>Place two or three fingertips on the CV6 point below the navel.</li>
      <li>Apply gentle, warm pressure in a clockwise circular motion.</li>
      <li>Breathe deeply into your lower abdomen for 2— minutes.</li>
      <li>Repeat once or twice daily, preferably in the morning.</li>
    </ol>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Science &amp; Research</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2019 study in <em>Journal of Acupuncture and Meridian Studies</em> found that CV6 moxibustion (heat therapy) improved immune function markers in older adults with chronic fatigue.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31182209/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1</a></sup> Research in <em>BMC Gastroenterology</em> showed that CV6 acupressure reduced bloating and improved bowel regularity in IBS patients.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29649994/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2</a></sup></p>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2021 systematic review in <em>Medicine</em> found that CV6 stimulation improved quality of life and reduced fatigue in cancer survivors undergoing rehabilitation.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33832049/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3</a></sup></p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Precautions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Avoid during pregnancy:</strong> CV6 stimulation is generally avoided during pregnancy.</li>
      <li>Do not apply pressure over full bladder or immediately after heavy meals.</li>
      <li>Avoid if you have abdominal surgery scars or hernias in the area.</li>
      <li>Use gentle pressure ?the abdomen is sensitive, especially after surgery.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Related Points</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">CV6 works well with <a href="/points/st36-zusanli-acupressure-point">ST36 (Zusanli)</a> for overall Qi boosting. For reproductive health, combine with <a href="/points/sp6-sanyinjiao-acupressure-point">SP6 (Sanyinjiao)</a> and <a href="/points/kd3-taixi-acupressure-point">KD3 (Taixi)</a>.</p>
  </section></article>
